                        "sense_id": "97dfc00b-2bef-3cb8-80df-57d09b75510e",
                        "entry_id": "1c38a94a-9e04-32a0-9dcd-c2f9b11477ce",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A chink; a rift."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "abf4e860-97eb-4343-8994-cc98b8f4565f",
                                "sense_id": "97dfc00b-2bef-3cb8-80df-57d09b75510e",
                                "text": "If thou mayest finde any shore,\nOr hole , or reft , what ever it were"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2aeec3c6-1c53-4c11-a177-b6f69e36c434",
                                "sense_id": "97dfc00b-2bef-3cb8-80df-57d09b75510e",
                                "text": "At one time the summit was beautifully bathed in golden light, whilst the middle part was quite blue, and the snow of its peculiar blue-green colour in the refts. Some of the glaciers are very distinct to us, and with the telescope I can see the refts and corrugations of the different parts, and the edges from which avalanches have fallen […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e97ff68-1f19-4f88-9b6c-b37c19dfcc0a",
                                "sense_id": "97dfc00b-2bef-3cb8-80df-57d09b75510e",
                                "text": "1894, Ivan Dexter, Talmud: A Strange Narrative of Central Australia, published in serial form in Port Adelaide News and Lefevre's Peninsula Advertiser (SA), Chapter VII, http://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks16/1600641.txt\nNow and again through a reft in the smoke a gleam of sunshine could be seen striking the rocks on the great peak to the west, but it had little or no effect in the gorge."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
